description:
Design a 2-to-4 line decoder. The module takes a 2-bit input and generates a corresponding 4-bit output, where only one of the output lines is activated (set to HIGH) based on the input combination. This decoder can be used in various applications like address decoding in memory systems or control signal generation in digital systems. The output is updated on the rising edge of the clock signal to ensure synchronization with other circuit components.
module top_module(
    input [1:0] in,
    input clk,
    output reg [3:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [1:0] in,
    input clk,
    output reg [3:0] out
);reg [3:0] out_reg;

always @(*) begin
    case(in)
        2'b00: out_reg = 4'b0001;
        2'b01: out_reg = 4'b0010;
        2'b10: out_reg = 4'b0100;
        2'b11: out_reg = 4'b1000;
        default: out_reg = 4'b0000; // default case to avoid latch inference
    endcase
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
    out <= out_reg;
end

endmodule

