description:
Design a clock phase shifter module that generates a clock signal with a variable phase shift. The module takes an input clock and a 4-bit phase shift amount; it uses a counter to count clock cycles and toggles the output clock phase whenever the counter matches the specified phase shift amount. This allows for dynamic adjustment of clock phases in digital circuits, which can be useful for timing adjustments and synchronization purposes.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [3:0] phase_shift_amount,
  output reg clk_phase_shifted
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [3:0] phase_shift_amount,
  output reg clk_phase_shifted
);reg [3:0] counter;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  counter <= counter + 1;
  if (counter == phase_shift_amount) begin
    counter <= 0;
    clk_phase_shifted <= ~clk_phase_shifted;
  end
end

endmodule

